Verse 1:
[Ab]What a fellowship, [Bbm/Db]what [Db]a [Ab]joy divine,
[Ab]Leaning on [Eb]the [Ab]everlasting arms;
[Bbm/Db]What a blessedness, [Ab/Eb]what a [Eb7]peace [Ab/Eb]is [Eb7]mine,
[Ab]Leaning on the everlasting [Db]arms.

Refrain:
[Ab]Leaning, leaning,
[Ab]safe and secure [Eb]from [Ab]all alarms;
[Db]leaning, leaning,
[Ab/Eb]leaning on the [Eb7]everlasting [Ab]arms.

Verse 2:
[Ab]O how sweet to [Bbm/Db]walk in [Db]this [Ab]pilgrim way,
[Ab]leaning on [Eb]the [Ab]everlasting arms;
[Bbm/Db]O how bright [Db]the [Ab/Eb]path grows from [Eb7]day [Ab/Eb]to [Eb7]day,
[Ab]leaning on the everlasting [Db]arms.

Verse 3:
[Ab]What have I to [Bbm/Db]dread, what [Db]have [Ab]I to fear,
[Ab]leaning on [Eb]the [Ab]everlasting arms?
[Bbm/Db]I have blessed [Db]peace [Ab/Eb]with my [Eb7]Lord so near,
[Ab]leaning on the everlasting [Db]arms.
